# A wayside boulder: one dome, uneven on purpose.
# Y is up, +Z is the way the creature faces, one world unit is one map tile.
# The lowest vertex sits on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0,
# so the game places it by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# Eyes are not modelled. They are two depth tested dots in the 2D layer, which
# is a pixel each instead of eight triangles.
#
# About 0.44 units tall and twice that across, 18 triangles.
# The base ring sits on the ground and is left open. Nothing above the
# horizon can see into it, and this is scenery that gets drawn a lot.

mtllib rock.mtl

# boulder, 18 triangles
v 0.000 0.440 0.000
v 0.324 0.300 0.000
v 0.135 0.300 0.218
v -0.165 0.300 0.267
v -0.276 0.300 0.000
v -0.159 0.300 -0.257
v 0.141 0.300 -0.228
v 0.432 0.000 0.000
v 0.253 0.000 0.400
v -0.202 0.000 0.320
v -0.497 0.000 0.000
v -0.221 0.000 -0.349
v 0.244 0.000 -0.386
usemtl rock_light
f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
f 1 4 5
f 1 5 6
f 1 6 7
f 1 7 2
usemtl rock_body
f 2 8 9 3
f 3 9 10 4
f 4 10 11 5
f 5 11 12 6
f 6 12 13 7
f 7 13 8 2
